/obj/item/readable/doctor
	icon_state = "white"
	name = "Medicine 101"
	txt = "<font size=25><B>A very fucking basics of medicine</B></font><HR>\n<BR>\n<B>How2change handz???</B><HR>\nWell, there're three kinds of damage: burn, brute and organ. Burns usually come from acids, hot gases and fire, brute - from bashing people with fists or something heavy or sharp enough, organ - from intoxication or drug overdose.<BR>\nThe following crap will help you to deal with crippled fuckers:<BR>\n<B>Body scanner</B>. It'll show to you how fucked the person is. Also detects epilepsy and chronic depression.<BR>\n<B>Blood analyzer.</B> Shows all of the chemicals in one's bloodstream. Vital for detecting intoxication.<BR>\n<B>CNS scanner.</B> Shows how fucked up your patient in his head. Psychiatrist can just look at somebody with the same effect due to his aura-seeking glasses applied to uniform.<BR>\n<B>Stamp and recipes.</B> You can forge (or re-forge) recipe with your stamp to precipt anything avaible in local drugstores. Drugstores are full of... uh... drugs: from absolutely harmless to dangerously addictive to toxic as heck so be careful. Also, you can re-forge any recipe only 2 times (1 time in case of already forged recipes), so don't even try to be greedy.<BR>\n<B>Regenerite.</B> If injected, heals organ damage greatly, as well as a bit of brute damage. You can splash naked people with it for instahealing of burn and brute damage. Emergenecy syringes contains some of this stuff.<BR>\n<B>ASD-F0. Those dark red pills can be used to restore some brute damage, if you're too greedy to splash people with iodine or regenerite. Oh, and about regenerite: ASD-F0/regenerite mix becomes toxic in one's bloodstream, so don't combine these drug. This stuff is also toxic when ODed (10+ pts), but getting rid of brute damage is worth the risks, right? Not to be confused with common ASD (without F0)!</B>\n<B>Antidote.</B> Slowly heals organ damage and removes majority of horrible toxins. Useless against overdose of all of the drugs except atropine and titbit.<BR>\n<B>Fibgenerite.</B> A somewhat expensive burn/wounds treatment drug. It is as powerful as a steamroller, and can be either splashed for massive chunk of burn instaheal or shot/drank for curing burns, open wounds and a small bit of brute and organ damage.<BR>\n<B>Manganeska.</B> A.K.A. potassium permanganate. Poor man's antidote. Removes toxic crap and cures nausea, but doesn't heal organ damage. Also works against codeine and morphine OD. Can be producted en masse by chemist.<BR>\n<B>Mangadote.</B> Antidote+. Almost twice as effective as antidote. You can feed some of it to chemist who just ate 9001pts of codeine as well.<BR>\n<B>Ambrosine.</B> Rapidly heals all kinds of damage, but only if you're feeling euphoria. Way more powerful against regenerite, but patient should jerk off and shoot drugs to make ambrosine work.<BR>\n<B>Antipsychotics.</B> Namely haloperidol, aminazine and clozapine. Removes potent stimulants (speed, meth, MDPV), psychedelics (including MDA and MDMA), dissociatives (including salvia) and deliriants (including atropine) from ones bloodstream, as well as lowing psychosis and curing delirium. Cures brain receptors when injected in huge doses, so cognitologists with 2+ receptor damage may require some of this crap. Keep in mind what antipsychotic OD will harm patient, however. And yes, it is psychiatrist's job to save motherfucker who just drank a whole bottle of DOB solution.<BR>\n<B>Epilepsy treatment.</B> Epilepsy may pop out after head prothesing or after a good punch in your ugly face. All of the benzos, as well as gabapentin, carbamazepine and barbi will cure this annoying crap. If you're too lazy, you can ask somebody to call a psychiatrist so he'll stuff patient with 9001 pills of phenazepam.<BR>\n<B>Glucose.</B><HR> Delicious stuff able to cure ethanol and methanol OD as well as addiction to sedatives of all kinds. Yep, you can feed glucose to junkies so they will be no longer on opiate hangover. Oh, and I forgot to say what psychiatrist have a crapload of glucose, so you can just call for this lazy-ass.<BR>\n<B>Antidepressants.</B><HR> A stuff for curing dysphoria and dysthymia (a.k.a. chronic depression). Dysthymia is a common side-effect of strong pain (i.e. from acid or neurowhip) or long-term crappy feeling (i.e. from delirium). There're several kinds of antidepressants, but fluoxetine is the most common. Psychiatrist starts with a fuckload of fluoxetine, so it is a good idea to call for this fucker in case of chronically depressed patients.<BR>\n<B>Benzodiazepines.</B><HR> A drugs which can cure epilepsy, remove delirium, calm patient down and do a lot of useful shit. Fucking addictive so be careful. You start with a phenazepam and can precipt it to anybody using your stamp since all drugstores have some of pzepam in their stocks.<BR>\n<B>Piracetam.</B><HR> Our fellow junk... cognitologists sometimes use it to soften the trip. 20+ of it have a chance of healing damaged brain receptors<BR>\n<B>Phenibut and phenotropil.</B><HR> Euphoretic GABA drugs what some med abusers will use if they feel saaaaaaaaad. Can heal damaged brain receptors, but only if ODed.<BR>\n<B>Dextroamitriptine.</B><HR> One pill or injection is enough to fully cure folk from stimulators or tobacco addiction.<BR>\n<B>ASD. A mysterious drug able to cure your fellow patient of any mutations, whenever he wants it or not. Toxic when ODed (5+ pts). Not to be confused with ASD-F0!</B>\n\n<B></B>\n<BR>\n<B>Prothesing for dummies.</B><HR>\nOh, c'mon, it is fucking easy.<BR>\n1)Pull poor legless fucker to the medbay.<BR>\n2)Inject him with prothesine (you have a bottle of it in biomechanics lab).<BR>\n3)Stick a severed limb or head to the body. If you can't find patient's leg, don't worry: you can forge prosthesises in biomechanics. Or cut off some fucktard's limb with scalpel and stick it to your patient.<BR>\n<BR>\n<B>Robotics 101</B><HR>\n1)Carry the corpse to biomechanics.<BR>\n2)Gib the body by pulling it over the gibber and activating this horrible piece of machinery.<BR>\n3)Cut the head open with the scalpel. You can do it on living person (yes, people CAN live with severed head, thanks to USSR-4 noospheric channeling) severed head as well which results in returning him normal vision.<BR>\n4)Put the brain inside the brainpod.<BR>\n5)Find or fabricate a pod stand, then put the brainpod on it. Your robot is ready, but it is immobile so it can only sweat about your mom and punch you if you're standing too close to it.<BR>\n6)Fabricate robotic jets and add it to your robot so he'll able to float around.<BR>\n<BR>\n<B>How to survive?</B><HR>\n1)Haloperidol injection will result in short-term stun. Injecting rampaging fuckers with it is good, but syringe gun is even better.<BR>\n2)Your scalpel may be not as powerful as axes or security whip, but it is sharp and can cut off heads and limbs, crippling your opponent.<BR>\n3)Chemists can make a crapload of horrible toxins and drugs for you. Shoot some speed and inject that traitor with plus-axe with 5 pts of DOB.<BR>\n4)Oh, and you can use trigan-D, dimedrol and other delirious shit! Ask the chemist to make a single huge DPH pill out of some dimedrol blisters, then force-feed it to stunned fucker. Hilarity ensures.<BR>\n5)Syringe gun darts! They can't be used for instainjection, but they can hold either up to 8 or up to 10 (2 common syringes) pts of horrible chemicals. You have a few prepared stundarts filled with barbiturates from the start, so you're on your own in means of finding godawful venoms to shoot people with.<BR>\n6)You can precipt any kind of medicine to yourself, from very useful (fibgen blisters and emergency syringes) to trippy as fuck. The chemist can forge for you a syringe dart of huge dose of tramadol/codeine/any other opiate so you can seriously OD fuckers with your syringe gun.<BR>\n"

