/obj/item/readable/designer
	name = "Wonderful world of designer drugs"
	txt = "<font size=20>Wonderful world of designer drugs</font>\n<BR><BR>\n<I>By Wasilisa Karlova and Ivan Rubershtaizer, edited by Jane Silvertooth</I>\n<BR><BR>\nWhere even to start it? Well, in case you have lived under the rock: for last centuries, not only government-corporations, but even USSR-4 had relatively liberal drug policy. However, while most of the soviet citizens take psychoactive substations on a less or more regular basis, having wrong drug in a wrong time on your hands will lead to inprisonment or even execution delivered by soviet militia. To avoid it, chemists sometimes invent (or re-invent, or steal) a drug which fucks you up for good while not being blacklisted by local government-corp drug agency nor being in a list of USSR-4 regulated preparations. Soviets are fast to adapt so they usually put any new psychoactive substation in a list of so-called \"research chemicals\": it means that cognis will chew on this chem until drowning in fractals to death or something and that civilian can't buy this drug with ease, but having some of the stuff in your pocket is still okay... at least, for now. So, designer drugs are legal while still kicking. Neat.\n<BR>\nThe problem is that we usually know nothing about those chemicals. Not like we know anything 'bout acid or 2C-B, but designer drugs are complete terra incognita: even if we had knew anything about them, we have forgotten it a long time ago. Take and synth them at your very own risk: while we'll try to guide you, we actually know little about this stuff, not unlike anybody else around.\n<BR><BR>\n<B>Zwerg drugs</B>\n<BR><BR>\nA.k.a. \"dwarven drugs\" (yet calling zwerg a \"dwarf\" will get you punched in the groin). Zwergs are the only non-human creatures USSR-4 xenopsychologists consider a power worthly to deal with diplomacy, since Zwerghelm is a fucking planetwide military factory and, after all, their society can be described as \"socialistic\" in most of the aspects. So soviets are okay with zwerg outposts popping around their \"bluespace oasises\", while zwergs are fine with commie junkies floating around in their ramshackle cans (so-called \"frontier stations\").\nZwergs are notorious not only for being short, sturdy creatures fond of drink and industry. They also have synthesed at least four extremely bizzare drugs suitable (he-he, \"suitable\") for human consumption. They don't mass-product the stuff, however: zwergs prefer good old ethanol, and it is unlikely that any other drugs hit them in the same manner as us. And even if they do, zwergs cannot into cognitology due to some flaw in their psychological mechanisms, so they can't make much of a use from drugs anyway. However, we have some info onto this stuff, albeit it is scarce and nebulous.\n<BR><BR>\nShining powder<BR>\nAn extremely weird phenethylamine drug. Excretes outta your blood at a rate of 0.3-0.6 per chemtick. Probably, works as a stimulant (and may be addictive), through its potency as a serotonin agonist may make it work as a psychedelic or antidepressant. Produced via mixing benzaldehyde, phenethylamine and some metal (albeit, we don't know what exact metal is needed). Reaction may require heating. Potential antidotes include benzos, neuroleptics and alkali metals, but we aren't sure about neither of these. Better not risk and test it with a smaller dosages (2pts or so) first.\n<BR><BR>\nMysterious powder<BR>\nYep. We know that it sounds extremely dumb, but absolutely every person will describe this powder as \"mysterious\". I've even asked a zwerg about this weird cognitive effect, but he just started to laugh like crazy instead of answering.\nAnyway, the stuff is, probably, some creepy psychedelic of tryptamine family, althrough there're rumours that it actually works as a prodrug for DMT, adrenochrome, some subkind of JWH or even ambrosine. And some folks will say you that it also works as antidepressant (not unlike most trypts anyway), a painkiller and good for lessening tension while on withdrawal from some junk. Made from a mixture of DiPT, some nootropic drug (all we know is that phenibut wouldn't work) and, again, from some metal we don't know. May or may not require heating up to 1. Neuroleptics always work fine as an antidote, effectiveness of benzos and widespread antidotes (such as manganeska or soviet \"blue antidote\") may vary.\n<BR><BR>\nGloomy powder<BR>\nThis is that will happen you mix two \"benzos\": benzodiazepine and benzaldehyde together and then add something else. What exactly? Well, we know that it is metallic. What else we know? We know that mixture may require heating and that some poor fools think that the stuff is a magical panacea against burns,, anxiety, epilepsy, pain, withdrawal-induced tension and even wounds. Obviously, you shouldn't believe into it without inspection. We're suspicious that gloomy powder actually works like a prodrug for ambrosine, just mildly euphoretic and with lots and lots of side-effects, be it beneficial or not.\nBoth benzos and neuros are completely useless if you've ODed on this drug, so try some other antidotes. \"Blue antidote\", manganeska or mangadote may work in this case.\n<BR><BR>\nPowder of wonders<BR>\nYes, this is how we call it. The stuff is an extremely powerful prodrug, but we don't know which exactly drug this thing will metabolize into. It may be some psychedelic stuff, ambrosine, mephedrone, all of the above at the same time or nothing of it at all. Its reaction include DMT and ambrosine as an ingredients. There's another ingredient, however: all that we know is that it is quite a potent and expensive medicine used by military medics or in emergency cases. And, as usual, reaction may require heating your mix a bit. We dunno what exactly works as an antidote to this powder, but we know that this antidote is widespread in USSR-4.\n<BR><BR>\nEldritch powder<BR>\nThe stuff is the only drug outright forbidden on Zwerghelm. Yes, fucking zwergs who don't give a damn about drugs have forbidden this one exclusively. You wanna know more? We wanna know too, but zwergs don't like to talk about this one and we don't like getting our ribs broken by drunken alien midgets. The stuff may be anything: prodrug for some powerful stuff, potent antidepressant, it may be toxic or even mutagenic. You need some Nuclear titbit (we hope you know how to cook it) to make it. Second ingredient is a potent organic poison: we know it because we've seen one poor bastard dropping dead after trying precursors with his tongue. May or may not require heating. Yep, again. But this time you'll know that you did it right because THE SOLUTION WILL LOOK AT YOU. Yep, everything is this bad. Uh-oh.\nAlso, every zwerg knows that warpotoxin is an antidote to the eldritch powder. Seriously, it is like \"don't run with scissors\" for them.\n<BR><BR><BR>\n\n<B>Other stuff</B>\n<BR><BR>\nWeird drugs from USSR-4 \"research chemicals\" list. A good cogni probably will sell his firstborn son and his liver to get the stuff. Some of these chems were invented back on the Old Earth hundreds of years ago, then forgotten and re-invented only during last few decades or so thanks to rampant usage of F.U.E.L. for making shortcuts in synthesis. And some of the stuff was discovered only recently and not much better than zwerg drugs.\n<BR><BR>\nUSSR-4 research benzodiazepines - a.k.a. \"cognibenzos\". They hit like a truck, have tiny dosages, derived from some potent \"non-research\" benzo and, basically, that's all we know about them. Cosmozepam was around for a while, yet there're whispers about extremely powerful soviet benzo called \"cognitozepam\".\n<BR><BR>\nFentanyl derivatives - there're loads and loads of them, yet acetylfentanyl is the most popular. Fentanyl itself is one of the very few drugs which will get you shot by police/militia anywhere sleevewide, since it is toxic enough to its possession being synonimous with walking around waving with a chemical warhead. Its derivatives are a bit more tame, but they're still potent opioids with tiny dosages. Acetic anhydride is your friend if you wanna make some yourself\n<BR><BR>\nMXE - as for now, MXE is not a \"research chemical\" and is a controlled drug instead, but let it be here for historical reasons. Most users will describe it as a ketamine, but twice as powerful at the same dosage. Producted by dropping some fuelsaccharose into 3-MeO-PCE, althrough good luck getting some at the first place.\n<BR><BR>\nMXP - some will say that MXP is similar to DXM, some - that it is similar to MXE. Actually, MXP is neither of it. This potent dissociative have some serotonergic properties, so beware of serotonin syndrome. The stuff is probably producted from 3-MeO-PCP the same way MXE is producted from 3-MeO-PCE.\n<BR><BR>\nSynthetic cannabinoids - weird stuff from smoking mixes. JWH family is well-known, not listed as a \"research chemical\" and relatively tame (althrough still toxic in large dosages). Shit happens then some nuthead start to experiment with adamantane: AB-228 is a \"poor man's JWH\" derived from adamantane, and APICA and APINACA are its more potent derivatives. White widow is some of an oddity, since it is AB-228 derivative with potent sedative properties.\n<BR><BR>\nWarnipizine - synthetic cannabinoid with healing properties. Or so we told. We're short of info on this one, but I know that it is derived from adamantane\n<BR><BR>\n2C-P - probably, the only phenethylamine psychedelic which is listed as a \"research chemical\" in USSR-4. All we know is that it is quite potent and derived from 2C-H.\n<BR><BR>\nBromoflies and bromodragonflies - those are NOT a \"research chemicals\": having some in your pocket WILL get you beaten senselessly. The reason is simple: the only thing cognis know about 2C-flies is just how extremely toxic those babies are. They're usually made from 2C-X family drugs similar to NBOMes... probably. I never synthesed one myself and will not encourage you to do so.\n<BR><BR>\nWeird tryptamines - while most of trypts (such as DMT, shrooms or DiPT a.k.a. \"hallucinogen for blind people\") were around for a while, there're still some of the less-researched ones left. 5-MeO-DiPT is derived from DiPT, and psilocybin is used in 4-AcO-DMT production\n<BR><BR>\nNuclear titbit - a truly creepy drug which can be best described as \"euphoretic deliriant\". It is potent, toxic, mildly radioactive, and some folks even say that it makes you glow, althrough the latter is probably a bullshit. Zwergs produce it from a mixture of some deliriant and some radioactive stuff, probably not as a drug, but as a chemical weaponry.\n"

/obj/item/readable/designer

